    <string name="update_auto">Look for a new version automatically</string>
    <string name="update_auto_sub">SNC Camera looks at most every six hours when the app is opened. When there is a new version the gear in the camera glows and a card is shown at the top of Settings. Tap Update and the new version is downloaded and checked, and Android\'s installer opens – tap Update there (Android requires that last tap). Your photos and settings stay, and SNC Camera starts again by itself afterwards; if Android stops that, a notification to tap comes instead.</string>
    <string name="update_privacy">Checking shows your IP address to GitHub. Turn off automatic checking if you don\'t want that.</string>
    <string name="update_install_note">The update is installed on top of the app. Photos and settings are kept. Android asks whether you want to install.</string>
